Better: build buckets.

```kotlin
private fun orderBubblesByPanels(
    bubbles: List<Rect>,
    panels: List<Rect>,
    direction: ReadingDirection,
): List<Rect> {
    if (panels.size < 2 || bubbles.size < 2) return bubbles
    val buckets = MutableList(panels.size) { mutableListOf<Int>() }  // indices of bubbles
    val orphans = mutableListOf<Rect>()
    bubbles.forEach { bubble ->
        val centerX = bubble.centerX().toFloat()
        val centerY = bubble.centerY().toFloat()
        var target = panels.indexOfFirst { it.contains(centerX, centerY) }
        if (target < 0) {
            // нет панели, содержащей центр: берём максимальное перекрытие
            var bestIdx = -1
            var bestArea = 0L
            panels.forEachIndexed { i, p ->
                val inter = intersectionArea(p, bubble)
                if (inter > bestArea) { bestArea = inter; bestIdx = i }
            }
            target = bestIdx
        }
        if (target >= 0) buckets[target] += bubble else orphans += bubble
    }
    return buckets.flatMap { orderBubblesWithinPanel(it, direction) } + orderBubblesWithinPanel(orphans, direction)
}

private fun orderBubblesWithinPanel(rects: List<Rect>, direction: ReadingDirection): List<Rect> {
    if (rects.size < 2) return rects
    // вертикальный текст (манга): сверху вниз, при близких верхах — по X
    val heights = rects.map { it.height() }.sorted()
    val median = heights.getOrNull(heights.size / 2) ?: 1
    val tolerance = (median * BUBBLE_ROW_TOLERANCE).coerceAtLeast(1f)
    val rows = mutableListOf<MutableList<Rect>>()
    var rowTop = -1
    for (r in rects.sortedBy { it.top }) {
        if (rowTop < 0 || r.top - rowTop > tolerance) { rows += mutableListOf(r); rowTop = r.top }
        else rows.last() += r
    }
    return rows.flatMap { row ->
        when (direction) {
            RTL -> row.sortedByDescending { it.left + it.right }
            else -> row.sortedBy { it.left + it.right }
        }
    }
}
```

Wait — for VERTICAL direction (Japanese vertical manga), within a panel reading is top-to-bottom, and columns go right-to-left. The row grouping with tolerance based on median height: for vertical text bubbles are tall; grouping by top within tolerance of 0.6*height might merge distinct vertical columns. Hmm. For vertical, better: sort by top, and only group if tops are close (small tolerance). Let me use a smaller tolerance for vertical: e.g. tolerance = median * 0.25, or simply for VERTICAL sort strictly by (top, then X by direction) without row grouping. Simpler and matches manga: within a panel, vertical text blocks read top-to-bottom; ties by X.

Actually the existing orderRegions for "vertical" does exactly: sortedWith(compareBy(top).thenBy(left)). For vertical, use that. For RTL/LTR horizontal, use row-major.

