**Found the root cause** for the "page turns before text is recognized" bug:

Line 330-333: when the auto-read frame is busy (scan/OCR/speech), autoscroll only slows to 1/3 speed — it does NOT stop. The comment says "не полный стоп — лента чуть ползёт, глаз не бежит впереди голоса". So the page keeps scrolling while OCR is still working → the captured frame goes out of view, and text gets skipped.

Also for PagerViewer (line 340-343): the autoscroll turns pages every 2-12 seconds **regardless of autoReadFrameBusy** — it moves to the next page while the current frame is being recognized/spoken. That's exactly "текст себе нашел сканирует и в это время листает вниз не успев распознать и прочесть".

The user's fix request: "не листать дальше, пока кадр не доозвучен; дай ему па couple секунд".

So:
1. PagerViewer branch: if `autoReadActive && autoReadFrameBusy` → don't move to next page, just wait.
2. Webtoon branch: full stop while busy (not 1/3 speed).
3. Add a small settle delay after a frame completes before the next capture, so the viewer settles (a couple hundred ms) — "дай ему пару секунд".

